---
const origin = Astro.site?.origin ?? "https://www.jsolly.com";
---

<section class="py-8 md:py-4 max-w-3xl" aria-labelledby="about-this-site-heading">
	<h2
		id="about-this-site-heading"
		class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-text-primary font-heading tracking-tight mb-4"
	>
		About this site
	</h2>
	<p class="text-lg text-text-secondary leading-relaxed mb-4">
		jsolly.com is the personal website of John Solly, Health-IT Division CTO at
		Leidos. It is a small static site: who I am, how to reach me, and pointers
		to work I publish elsewhere. It is not a Leidos corporate page and it does
		not ship a product API.
	</p>
	<p class="text-lg text-text-secondary leading-relaxed mb-8">
		Most of my career has been building spatial systems — at Esri, startups, and
		federal agencies. I now lead technology strategy for Leidos' Health IT
		division, supporting agencies such as SSA, VA, and HHS. My focus is the
		convergence of spatial computing and AI: helping machines interpret the
		physical world and putting that to work on missions that matter.
	</p>

	<h3
		id="pages-on-this-site-heading"
		class="text-xl font-bold text-text-primary font-heading tracking-tight mb-3"
	>
		Pages
	</h3>
	<ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-lg text-text-secondary leading-relaxed mb-8 space-y-2">
		<li>
			<a href="/about/">About</a> — background, focus areas, and how I got here
		</li>
		<li>
			<a href="/contact/">Contact</a> — social profiles and a contact form
		</li>
		<li>
			<a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a> — data practices for this static site
		</li>
		<li>
			<a href="/John-Solly-Resume.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
				>Resume</a
			>
			(PDF)
		</li>
		<li>
			<a href="https://www.blogthedata.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
				>Blog</a
			>
			— writing lives on Blogthedata, not here
		</li>
	</ul>

	<h3
		id="for-agents-heading"
		class="text-xl font-bold text-text-primary font-heading tracking-tight mb-3"
	>
		For agents
	</h3>
	<p class="text-lg text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">
		Start at
		<a href={`${origin}/llms.txt`}>{origin}/llms.txt</a>
		for when-to-use guidance. Request any page with
		<code class="text-base">Accept: text/markdown</code>
		(or fetch the
		<code class="text-base">.md</code>
		sibling) to get a Markdown body without the layout chrome. Missing paths
		return HTTP 404 with recovery links to the sitemap and that index.
	</p>
</section>
